            "output": "<task id=\"ses_ef8d57280ffeAgx4MP4EvhkS4o\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Findings\n\nIssue [#3](https://github.com/itsmeyaw/binden/issues/3) requires CAPTCHA-free token verification, CAPTCHA-protected resend, distinct outcomes, a fixed 24-hour submission lifetime, and concurrency-safe lifecycle changes. Its dependency, issue #2, is closed and its schema/API foundation is present.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. **Extend persisted verification lifecycle**\n   - Update `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/schema.ts` and generate a Drizzle migration under `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/drizzle/`.\n   - Reuse `signupRequest.status`, `verificationTokenHash`, `verificationExpiresAt`, and `createdAt`.\n   - Add only fields necessary to distinguish consumed/expired state if status plus existing timestamps cannot do so safely; retain the original expiry when resending.\n\n2. **Centralize verification and resend operations**\n   - Add a small server module, likely `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/verification.ts`.\n   - Hash incoming tokens with the existing `node:crypto` SHA-256 pattern.\n   - Use conditional database updates (`pending_verification` + matching hash + unexpired) so exactly one competing verification succeeds and moves the request to `verified`.\n   - Resend accepts a normalized contact email plus a Turnstile token; verify Turnstile server-side using an action-aware extension of `verifyTurnstile`, rotate the stored token, and insert a replacement captured message without modifying `verificationExpiresAt`.\n\n3. **Expose public HTTP routes**\n   - Add `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/app/api/verify/route.ts` for token verification.\n   - Add `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/app/api/verify/resend/route.ts` for protected resend.\n   - Follow `createSignupHandler(overrides)` in `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/app/api/signup/route.ts` for injectable DB/Turnstile dependencies and no-store JSON responses.\n   - Preserve local mail capture through `mailMessage`; do not add a mail provider.\n\n4. **Add verification/resend UI**\n   - Add `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/app/verify/page.tsx`, backed by a focused client component if interaction requires it (for example, `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/components/verification-form.tsx`).\n   - Reuse existing shadcn `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/components/ui/{alert,button,card,field,input,spinner}.tsx` and the Turnstile widget pattern in `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/components/signup-form.tsx`.\n   - Render clear, distinct valid, expired, invalid, and already-used outcomes; give expired/invalid users a resend path.\n\n5. **Test behavior at the existing HTTP seam**\n   - Extend or rename `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/tests/signup.ts`; it is the only current test harness and uses `node:assert` plus injected route dependencies.\n   - Cover successful verification, invalid/expired/used tokens, CAPTCHA rejection before resend persistence, fixed expiry across resend, captured replacement URL, and parallel/repeated verify/resend conditional-update outcomes.\n\n## Existing patterns and dependencies\n\n- DB: Drizzle + Neon HTTP via `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/db.ts`; migrations configured by `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/drizzle.config.ts`.\n- Input validation: Zod in `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/signup.ts`.\n- CAPTCHA: `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/turnstile.ts` currently hard-codes action `\"signup\"`; it needs an explicit allowed action parameter for resend.\n- Mail capture: `mailMessage` records in `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/schema.ts`, gated by `MAIL_CAPTURE=true`.\n- Configuration to retain: `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/.env.example` (`DATABASE_URL`, `APP_URL`, Turnstile settings, `MAIL_CAPTURE`).\n\n## Risks / open questions\n\n- “Expired” versus “invalid” needs a retained lookup path: expired records must remain long enough to report expiry, while the parent spec also requires later cleanup of unverified submissions.\n- Resend identification is unspecified. A contact-email resend form is the natural public path, but its response should avoid exposing whether an email has an active request.\n- The existing `db.batch()` write model should be checked for conditional-update-plus-message atomicity; concurrent resends must not leave a delivered token that cannot succeed.\n- Existing untracked screenshots (`signup-01-layout.png`, `signup-01-mobile.png`) are unrelated and should remain untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\npnpm test\npnpm lint\npnpm format:check\npnpm build\npnpm exec drizzle-kit migrate\n```\n\nManual configured-environment check: submit a request, read its captured verification URL, verify it, then test resend with a valid Turnstile token and confirm the original 24-hour deadline remains unchanged.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
