              "subagent_type": "code-review",
              "prompt": "Review-only. Review git diff main...HEAD in /Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/.worktrees/issue-3-verify-request and commits f5bd563, 1e5ec07 against GitHub issue #3. Requirements: valid verification link verifies email with no CAPTCHA and becomes review-eligible; expired/invalid/already-used links have distinct clear applicant outcomes; resend requires successful server-side Turnstile and cannot extend 24-hour submission lifetime; repeated/competing verification/resend actions preserve one coherent persisted lifecycle outcome. Parent #1 additionally says resend response must avoid email enumeration and requests are deleted 24h after initial submission. Identify missing, wrong, or scope-creep behavior with severity and file:line. Do not edit. Under 400 words."
            },
            "output": "<task id=\"ses_ef8ca7ca1ffeaGezHbKJttJsNL\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Findings\n\n- **[P1] Expired requests are never deleted and can block reapplication** — `src/app/api/signup/route.ts:51`; `src/lib/schema.ts:19-23`  \n  The 24-hour deadline is only stored. Nothing in this change deletes expired submissions; their `pending_verification` status keeps them in the active-email unique index. After expiry, the applicant cannot submit a fresh request with the same email, contrary to parent #1’s deletion requirement and the reapplication flow.\n\n- **[P2] Used links can be reported as invalid after the request advances** — `src/app/api/verify/route.ts:45-52`  \n  The `used` outcome is returned only when status is exactly `verified`. Once a verified request advances to another lifecycle status (such as `under_review`), the same retained token falls through to `invalid`, so the applicant no longer gets the required distinct already-used outcome.\n\n- **[P2] Tests do not substantiate eligibility or concurrency behavior** — `tests/signup.ts:53-68, 71-107`  \n  The verification DB fake ignores all query predicates and returns preset rows; resend tests likewise don’t model expiry or competing updates. These tests pass, but do not verify the persisted lifecycle guards or the required repeated/competing-action behavior.\n\n## Checks\n\n`pnpm test` and `pnpm lint` pass. `pnpm format:check` fails on unchanged `.opencode/plugins/entire.ts`. No scope creep identified.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
